FORM S-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: statutes-of-trigonometry.
FILED BY: the land surveyor, whose instruments were confiscated at the bridge.

OFF THE RECORD: The statutes of trigonometry, tabulated. No IEEE float
OFF THE RECORD: exists in this jurisdiction, so the circle is divided
OFF THE RECORD: into 120 units of 3 arc-degrees each, and the sine of
OFF THE RECORD: every unit is entered in the table below, scaled by
OFF THE RECORD: 1000 and rounded to the nearest entry. Three figures
OFF THE RECORD: of precision; the Court measures angles the way it
OFF THE RECORD: measures everything, which is to say officially.
OFF THE RECORD:
OFF THE RECORD: Usage: claim the table once, on the record, and hand
OFF THE RECORD: it back with every petition. The offices hold no
OFF THE RECORD: records of their own, so the statutes stay reentrant:
OFF THE RECORD:
OFF THE RECORD:   LET IT BE RECORDED THAT table IS THE FINDING OF the-table-of-sines.
OFF THE RECORD:   PROCLAIM THE FINDING OF sine REGARDING 15 AND table.
OFF THE RECORD:
OFF THE RECORD: Angles may be any integer, positive or negative; the
OFF THE RECORD: offices reduce them to the circle. The cosine is the
OFF THE RECORD: sine a quarter turn ahead, as it always was.

THE OFFICE OF the-table-of-sines.
    REMAND WITH A SCHEDULE COMPRISING
        0 AND 52 AND 105 AND 156 AND 208 AND 259 AND 309 AND 358 AND
        407 AND 454 AND 500 AND 545 AND 588 AND 629 AND 669 AND 707 AND
        743 AND 777 AND 809 AND 839 AND 866 AND 891 AND 914 AND 934 AND
        951 AND 966 AND 978 AND 988 AND 995 AND 999 AND 1000 AND 999 AND
        995 AND 988 AND 978 AND 966 AND 951 AND 934 AND 914 AND 891 AND
        866 AND 839 AND 809 AND 777 AND 743 AND 707 AND 669 AND 629 AND
        588 AND 545 AND 500 AND 454 AND 407 AND 358 AND 309 AND 259 AND
        208 AND 156 AND 105 AND 52 AND 0 AND -52 AND -105 AND -156 AND
        -208 AND -259 AND -309 AND -358 AND -407 AND -454 AND -500 AND -545 AND
        -588 AND -629 AND -669 AND -707 AND -743 AND -777 AND -809 AND -839 AND
        -866 AND -891 AND -914 AND -934 AND -951 AND -966 AND -978 AND -988 AND
        -995 AND -999 AND -1000 AND -999 AND -995 AND -988 AND -978 AND -966 AND
        -951 AND -934 AND -914 AND -891 AND -866 AND -839 AND -809 AND -777 AND
        -743 AND -707 AND -669 AND -629 AND -588 AND -545 AND -500 AND -454 AND
        -407 AND -358 AND -309 AND -259 AND -208 AND -156 AND -105 AND -52.

THE OFFICE OF sine, CONCERNING angle AND table.
    REMAND WITH THE ITEM AT ((angle NOTWITHSTANDING 120 PLUS 120) NOTWITHSTANDING 120) PLUS 1 IN table.

THE OFFICE OF cosine, CONCERNING angle AND table.
    REMAND WITH THE FINDING OF sine REGARDING angle PLUS 30 AND table.
